Now part 3: getLightsData, getLights, and equals cases.

For equals I'll write a helper that creates an observer + render object and runs equals with renderId.

equals signature: equals(renderObject, lightsData, renderId).

Note: equals calls getRenderObjectData which may create data if missing. So first call establishes snapshot.

Let me write tests:

```js
describe('equals', () => {
  function setup(options = {}) { const renderObject = createRenderObject(options); const observer = createPlainObserver(); return { observer, renderObject }; }
```

Cases:

1. returns true for unchanged render object and keeps state in sync:
```js
const { observer, renderObject } = setup();
expect(observer.equals(renderObject, [], 1)).toBe(true);
expect(observer.equals(renderObject, [], 1)).toBe(true);
```

2. world matrix change:
```js
const { object } = renderObject;
object.position.set(1,0,0); object.updateMatrixWorld();
expect(observer.equals(ro, [], 2)).toBe(false);
expect(observer.equals(ro, [], 2)).toBe(true); // synced
```
Careful: 2nd call with same renderId 2: the worldMatrix check passes; material check: materialData._renderId === 2 already? On first call with renderId 2, materialData._renderId set to 2, no change. On second call with 2 → skipped. Returns true. Good.

3. material property change: detected, increments version, once per renderId:
```js
const { observer, renderObject, material } = ...
expect(observer.equals(ro, [], 1)).toBe(true);
material.opacity = 0.4;
expect(observer.equals(ro, [], 2)).toBe(false);
expect(observer.equals(ro, [], 2)).toBe(true);
// changes within the same render id are not observed again
material.opacity = 0.8;
expect(observer.equals(ro, [], 2)).toBe(true);
expect(observer.equals(ro, [], 3)).toBe(false);
```
Wait, careful on `material.opacity = 0.8` then equals(ro,[],2) → material check skipped (renderId 2), materialVersion matches → then returns true. Then equals(ro,[],3) → material check runs → opacity changed → version++ → materialVersion mismatch → false. Good.

4. shared material checked once per render but all render objects detect the change:
```js
const material = new MeshBasicMaterial();
const roA = createRenderObject({material});
const roB = createRenderObject({material});
observer.equals(roA, [], 1) → true
observer.equals(roB, [], 1) → true
material.opacity = 0.5;
expect(observer.equals(roA, [], 2)).toBe(false);
expect(observer.equals(roB, [], 2)).toBe(false);
```
Careful for roB: roB's snapshot data.materialVersion 0 vs materialData._version 1 → false. Good. But wait roB's materialData._renderId was set to 1 during its first equals; now with renderId 2 the material loop is skipped (already 2 from roA) and version mismatch → false. Good, this demonstrates shared-check semantics.

5. texture change: material.map set to texture; first equals → true? Careful: material data snapshot taken at getRenderObjectData → materialVersion 0. Then in equals(renderId 1): material loop compares data.map (null) with mtlValue (undefined? no, material.map = texture so mtlValue is texture). data.map === null and mtlValue not null → branch `value === null` → value !== mtlValue → set to {id, version, cacheVersion} and changed=true → _version 1 → mismatch → false. Hmm so first equals returns false. Let me design: set map before creating? getRenderObjectData will snapshot it. Then equals → true. Then texture.needsUpdate → version 1 → equals with renderId 2 → false. Then swap to a different texture → false.

6. buffer size change:
```js
renderObject.context.width = 1024;
expect(observer.equals(ro, [], 2)).toBe(false);
expect(observer.equals(ro, [], 2)).toBe(true);
```

7. geometry replacement:
```js
const newGeometry = new BufferGeometry();
ro.geometry = newGeometry;
expect(equals(...,2)).toBe(false);
```
Also geometry disposal → version bump → false.

8. attribute change: geometry.attributes.position.needsUpdate = true → false; then same renderId → true (once per render).

Wait: after detection, geometryData._renderId set to renderId and _version bumped; renderObjectData.geometryVersion synced. Next call same renderId → attributes not rechecked → true.

9. attribute removal: `geometry.deleteAttribute('position')` → false.

Hmm careful: after removal, attribute loop: storedAttributes has 'position' but attributes.position undefined → delete + changed → version++ → false. Good.

10. index and drawRange changes.

Combine into one test each for clarity.

11. morph target influences.

12. instancing: matrix version, color, morphTexture.

13. batching: matrices/indirect/colors textures.

14. lights: shadow map size change and spot map version/cacheVersion.

For lights I need renderObjectData.lights populated at init: renderObject with lightsNode containing lights, geometry etc. In equals, `lightsData` param is compared against `renderObjectData.lights`.

```js
const light = new DirectionalLight();
light.castShadow = true;
const lightsNode = createLightsNode([light]);
const ro = createRenderObject({ lightsNode });
const observer = createPlainObserver();
expect(observer.equals(ro, observer.getLightsData(lightsNode.getBuiltinLights(), []), 1)).toBe(true);
