to trigger, scene.environment must be non-null and material.envMap === null.
scene.environment = new Texture(); // hmm scene.environment setter may be defined
```
Check: Scene has `environment` property plain assignment? Let's grep. Also environmentIntensity setter? There's `set environmentIntensity`? Probably plain.

Then equals with renderId 1 → true. Then scene.environmentIntensity = 0.5 → false. Then true. Then scene.environmentRotation.set(0, Math.PI, 0) → false.

Then a test that environment changes are ignored when scene.environment is null or material has envMap:
```js
scene.environment = null → change intensity → true
material.envMap = texture (MeshBasicMaterial has envMap) → change intensity → true
```

16. center: Sprite; change center → false.

17. bundle: renderObject.bundle non-null — equals always sets version and returns true even when bundle version changed:
```js
const bundle = { version: 1, static: false };
const ro = createRenderObject({ bundle });
equals(ro, [], 1) → true, data.version 1 (already 1 from init)
bundle.version = 2;
equals(ro, [], 2) → true but renderObjectData.version becomes 2
check observer.getRenderObjectData(ro).version === 2
```

Let's now write part 3 (getLightsData, getLights, equals). Keep it moderate.

getLightsData:
```js
const observer = createPlainObserver();
expect(observer.getLightsData([], [])).toEqual([]);

// ambient/plain lights are ignored
const ambient = new AmbientLight();
expect(observer.getLightsData([ambient], [])).toEqual([]);

// shadow casting lights record shadow map size
const directional = new DirectionalLight();
directional.castShadow = true;
expect(observer.getLightsData([directional], [])).toEqual([{shadowMapWidth:512, shadowMapHeight:512}]);

// spot light maps
const spot = new SpotLight();
spot.map = new Texture();
expect(observer.getLightsData([spot], [])).toEqual([{map:0, cacheVersion:0}]);

// combined
spot.castShadow = true;
expect(...).toEqual([{map:0, cacheVersion:0, shadowMapWidth:512, shadowMapHeight:512}]);

// resets the provided array
const lights = [{stale:true}];
observer.getLightsData([directional], lights) → length 1 and equals expected
```
Careful: `new SpotLight()` default castShadow false. `ambient.castShadow`? AmbientLight has no shadow property, castShadow undefined → skipped; also shadow undefined.

Also for spot light with castShadow: SpotLight has shadow → shadow.mapSize (512,512).

getLights caching:
```js
const lightsNode = createLightsNode([directional]);
const first = observer.getLights(lightsNode, 1);
expect(first).toEqual([{shadowMapWidth:512,...}]);
expect(observer.getLights(lightsNode, 1)).toBe(first);
// new render id recomputes in place
directional.shadow.mapSize.set(1024,1024);
const second = observer.getLights(lightsNode, 2);
expect(second).toBe(first);
expect(second).toEqual([{shadowMapWidth:1024, shadowMapHeight:1024}]);
```
Good — shows in-place mutation.

Note module-level `_lightsCache` is keyed by lightsNode; fresh node per test.

